  "2026-07-14T22:56:40.012Z",codex-root,"Live Scorecard code-scanning reconciliation 2026-07-15: alerts #17-#23 map to existing children pm-003j (3 Token-Permissions instances), pm-0yi7 (Fuzzing), pm-2d7k (Security-Policy), pm-obq2 (Code-Review), and pm-rrt1 (CII-Best-Practices). No duplicate items created; these remain outside the active SDK implementation bundle."
  "2026-07-17T13:31:46.710Z",codex-root,"Live GitHub reconciliation 2026-07-17: no open PRs, Dependabot alerts, or secret-scanning alerts. Scorecard alerts #17-#23 remain exactly mapped to existing children pm-003j (Token-Permissions x3), pm-0yi7 (Fuzzing), pm-2d7k (Security-Policy), pm-obq2 (Code-Review), and pm-rrt1 (CII-Best-Practices); no duplicate item created. Current main head d56632fe has green CI, CodeQL, Security and Script Quality, OSSF Scorecard, and CodSpeed runs."
  "2026-07-21T16:53:27.606Z",codex-derived-context-20260721,"Live GitHub Scorecard reconciliation 2026-07-21: code scanning has exactly 7 open OSSF Scorecard alerts, still mapped to canonical children pm-003j (Token-Permissions x3), pm-0yi7 (Fuzzing), pm-2d7k (Security-Policy), pm-obq2 (Code-Review), and pm-rrt1 (CII-Best-Practices). Dependabot alerts=0, secret-scanning alerts=0, and pnpm audit vulnerabilities=0 at every severity. No duplicate security item created."
  "2026-07-25T18:18:14.300Z","harness:codex","Live GitHub reconciliation 2026-07-25: open PRs=0; 21 open issues all have owner-authored links to canonical pm items; Dependabot alerts=0; secret-scanning alerts=0; pnpm audit reports 0 vulnerabilities at every severity. Code scanning has 8 open OSSF Scorecard reports: existing alerts #17-#23 remain mapped to pm-003j (Token-Permissions x3), pm-0yi7 (Fuzzing), pm-2d7k (Security-Policy), pm-obq2 (Code-Review), and pm-rrt1 (CII-Best-Practices); new alert #32 is another auto-release Token-Permissions instance owned by pm-003j, so no duplicate item was created. Main head d1d0e860 has green CI, CodeQL, Security and Script Quality, OSSF Scorecard, and CodSpeed runs. These items remain open and unclaimed because the active implementation bundle is SDK/CLI agent identity."
  "2026-07-26T13:16:19.177Z","harness:codex","Live GitHub security reconciliation 2026-07-26: Dependabot alerts=0, secret-scanning alerts=0, and pnpm audit vulnerabilities=0. Code scanning now has exactly two open OpenSSF Scorecard reports: #20 Code-Review (high), already owned by canonical pm-obq2, and #22 CII-Best-Practices (low), already owned by canonical pm-rrt1. Both are repository/community policy gaps rather than source vulnerabilities; no duplicate security item created. All 30 open GitHub issues have an owner-authored .agents/pm item link."
  "2026-07-27T02:37:56.182Z","harness:codex","Live GitHub security reconciliation after v2026.7.27: npm audit has zero known vulnerabilities; Dependabot and secret-scanning have zero open alerts; Sentry has zero critical/high issues; and exact merged-main security, CodeQL, Scorecard, Trivy, TruffleHog, Semgrep, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, and actionlint gates passed. The only code-scanning entries were Scorecard governance meters #20 and #22, mapped to pm-obq2 and pm-rrt1. They were dismissed as wont-fix scanner instances because their remaining remediation is respectively a second trusted human maintainer and authorized bestpractices.dev attestation; both canonical PM items remain open and unclaimed, so the limitations are not represented as completed."
  "2026-08-07T08:08:07.887Z","harness:codex","Live Scorecard reconciliation 2026-08-07 for PR #927: code-scanning alerts #35 CITestsID (low) and #28 SASTID (medium) are rolling-history governance meters, not source vulnerabilities. Their own evidence says current CI/SAST exists but only 10/11 recent merged PRs and 14/19 recent commits were recognized; exact head 9ad9138e3 passed four coverage shards plus aggregator, static/smoke/compat/typecheck/Windows jobs, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, and all security gates. The missed history cannot be repaired without rewriting immutable commits and will age out as PR-only protected merges continue. Both scanner instances are therefore accepted under this program and dismissed as wont-fix historical-window instances, while pm-u1baah and pm-5zca retain the actual direct-push/branch-protection work open and unclaimed."
